</head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to main content</a><header class="site-header" data-site-header><div class="site-header__inner shell"><a class="brand-link" href="/" aria-label="NovaDot home"><img class="brand-logo" src="/brand/novadot-full-logo-footer-transparent.png" srcset="/brand/novadot-full-logo-footer-transparent.png 1x, /brand/novadot-full-logo-footer-transparent-2x.png 2x" width="720" height="280" alt="NovaDot"></a><nav class="desktop-nav" aria-label="Primary navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/services/">Services</a><a href="/events/">Events &amp; Space</a><a href="/how-we-work/" aria-current="page">How We Work</a><a href="/about/">About</a></nav><a class="button button--primary header-cta" href="/contact/">Discuss your project</a><button class="menu-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Open navigation menu" aria-controls="mobile-navigation" aria-expanded="false" data-menu-toggle><span aria-hidden="true"></span><span aria-hidden="true"></span><span aria-hidden="true"></span></button></div></header><nav id="mobile-navigation" class="mobile-nav" aria-label="Mobile navigation" hidden data-mobile-nav><div class="shell mobile-nav__inner"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/services/">Services</a><div class="mobile-nav__services" role="group" aria-label="Service areas"><a href="/services/software-ai-business-systems/">Software, AI &amp; Business Systems</a><a href="/services/web-mobile-digital-growth/">Web, Mobile &amp; Digital Growth</a><a href="/services/cloud-security-it-operations/">Cloud, Security &amp; IT Operations</a></div><a href="/events/">Events &amp; Space</a><a href="/how-we-work/" aria-current="page">How We Work</a><a href="/about/">About</a><a href="/contact/">Contact</a><a class="button button--primary" href="/contact/">Discuss your project</a></div></nav><script type="module">var e=document.querySelector(`[data-menu-toggle]`),t=document.querySelector(`[data-mobile-nav]`);if(e instanceof HTMLButtonElement&&t instanceof HTMLElement){let n=[document.querySelector(`.skip-link`),document.querySelector(`main`),document.querySelector(`footer`)].filter(e=>e instanceof HTMLElement),r=e=>{n.forEach(t=>{t.inert=e})},i=(n=!1)=>{let i=e.getAttribute(`aria-expanded`)===`true`;e.setAttribute(`aria-expanded`,`false`),e.setAttribute(`aria-label`,`Open navigation menu`),t.hidden=!0,document.body.classList.remove(`menu-open`),r(!1),n&&i&&e.focus()};e.addEventListener(`click`,()=>{let n=e.getAttribute(`aria-expanded`)!==`true`;e.setAttribute(`aria-expanded`,String(n)),e.setAttribute(`aria-label`,n?`Close navigation menu`:`Open navigation menu`),t.hidden=!n,document.body.classList.toggle(`menu-open`,n),r(n)}),t.querySelectorAll(`a`).forEach(e=>e.addEventListener(`click`,()=>i())),document.addEventListener(`keydown`,n=>{if(n.key===`Escape`&&i(!0),n.key===`Tab`&&e.getAttribute(`aria-expanded`)===`true`){let r=[e,...t.querySelectorAll(`a`)],i=r[0],a=r.at(-1);n.shiftKey&&document.activeElement===i?(n.preventDefault(),a?.focus()):!n.shiftKey&&document.activeElement===a&&(n.preventDefault(),i.focus())}}),window.matchMedia(`(min-width: 960px)`).addEventListener(`change`,e=>{e.matches&&i()})}</script><main id="main-content"><section class="page-hero page-hero--compact"><div class="shell page-hero__compact-inner"><div class="page-hero__copy"><p class="eyebrow">How we work</p><h1>Start with the decision, not the build.</h1><p class="page-hero__lead">We define the problem and its consequence, compare lower-risk options and scope only the change that can be delivered and supported responsibly.</p></div></div></section><section class="content-section" aria-label="Delivery stages" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><div class="shell stage-ledger" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><article class="work-stage" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><h2 data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>1. Understand what you need</h2><p data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>We review your goals, the current system, the people affected and any constraints. Together, we agree what to prioritise.</p></article><article class="work-stage" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><h2 data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>2. Compare the options</h2><p data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>We evaluate repairing what exists, configuring supported products, integrating systems or commissioning custom work.</p></article><article class="work-stage" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><h2 data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>3. Agree the scope and responsibilities</h2><p data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Before work starts, we agree the deliverables, dependencies, responsibilities, approval checks, ownership, data export and handover arrangements.</p></article><article class="work-stage" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><h2 data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>4. Deliver, hand over and support</h2><p data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>We review progress and agree release and handover checks. Any ongoing support has a defined scope, coverage and response expectations.</p></article></div></section><section class="content-section content-section--porcelain" aria-labelledby="client-inputs-title" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><div class="shell content-grid" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><p class="content-grid__aside" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Client inputs</p><div class="prose" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><h2 id="client-inputs-title" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>What we need from you</h2><ul class="input-list" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>A named decision owner.</li><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Safe access to representative information.</li><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Availability from the people who use or own the workflow.</li><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Known constraints, deadlines and incumbent suppliers.</li><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>An agreed way to give feedback and approve completed work.</li></ul></div></div></section><section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="ai-worksheet-title" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><div class="shell" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><div class="section-heading-grid" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><div data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><p class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Practical scoping worksheet</p><h2 id="ai-worksheet-title" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Choose one task for an AI or automation pilot</h2></div><div class="section-heading__aside" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><p data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Start with a repeated task you can describe and check. Record what comes in, what a useful output looks like, who reviews it and what would count as an improvement.</p></div></div><div class="worksheet-grid" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><div class="worksheet-card" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><span class="field-number" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>01</span><h3 data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Current task &amp; frequency</h3><p class="field-desc" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>A specific, repeated manual step and how often it happens.</p><div class="field-example" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><span class="example-label" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Example</span><p data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Matching incoming supplier invoice and receipt text records against open orders; 30–50 records weekly.</p></div></div><div class="worksheet-card" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><span class="field-number" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>02</span><h3 data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Input format &amp; source</h3><p class="field-desc" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Where the source material arrives from and in what format.</p><div class="field-example" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><span class="example-label" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Example</span><p data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Standard digital invoice or receipt text file placed into a designated intake folder.</p></div></div><div class="worksheet-card" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><span class="field-number" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>03</span><h3 data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Expected structured output</h3><p class="field-desc" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>The format needed for the next step or destination system.</p><div class="field-example" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><span class="example-label" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Example</span><p data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Structured summary CSV or draft form fields with unstated tax amounts flagged for human review.</p></div></div><div class="worksheet-card" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><span class="field-number" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>04</span><h3 data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Designated human reviewer</h3><p class="field-desc" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>The named role or person responsible for validating draft outputs.</p><div class="field-example" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><span class="example-label" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Example</span><p data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Named finance officer who approves drafts before ledger posting.</p></div></div><div class="worksheet-card" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><span class="field-number" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>05</span><h3 data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Sensitive exclusions</h3><p class="field-desc" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Confidential fields or personal data that must be redacted or omitted.</p><div class="field-example" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><span class="example-label" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Example</span><p data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Exclude customer bank details, staff payroll data, and proprietary pricing notes.</p></div></div><div class="worksheet-card" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><span class="field-number" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>06</span><h3 data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Measurable success check</h3><p class="field-desc" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>An objective standard to determine if the pilot delivered value.</p><div class="field-example" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><span class="example-label" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Example</span><p data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Reduction in rekeying time per batch with 100% of exception-flagged tax fields manually reviewed.</p></div></div></div><div class="worksheet-footer" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><p class="worksheet-note" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><strong data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Privacy note:</strong> You can work through these six fields internally before contacting anyone. No confidential files or proprietary data need to be uploaded to discuss your requirement.</p><a class="button button--secondary" href="/contact/?topic=workflow-pilot" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Discuss your workflow</a></div></div></section><section class="content-section content-section--porcelain" id="commercial-terms" aria-labelledby="commercial-terms-title" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><div class="shell" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><div class="section-heading-grid" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><div data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><p class="eyebrow" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Commercial process &amp; fees</p><h2 id="commercial-terms-title" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>How we agree scope, fees and commercial terms</h2></div><div class="section-heading__aside" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><p data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Tell us what you want to achieve, who uses the system and any deadline or constraints. If an assessment is needed, we will agree its scope and any fee before starting. The proposal will set out deliverables, responsibilities, acceptance checks and support arrangements.</p></div></div><div class="commercial-grid" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><div class="commercial-card" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><h3 data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>What influences price &amp; timing</h3><ul class="commercial-list" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><strong data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Data quality &amp; cleanliness:</strong> Moving structured, modern databases is faster and lower-risk than rescuing fragmented spreadsheets or undocumented legacy schemas.</li><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><strong data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Integration depth:</strong> Off-the-shelf connectors take less time than developing bespoke API adapters against legacy systems.</li><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><strong data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Standard vs custom:</strong> Configuring supported software (like Odoo or WordPress) is more cost-effective than building from scratch.</li><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><strong data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Review turnaround:</strong> Prompt feedback from your designated decision owner keeps delivery milestones on schedule.</li></ul></div><div class="commercial-card" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><h3 data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>How a project is phased</h3><ol class="phasing-list" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><strong data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>1. Discovery &amp; Assessment:</strong><span data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>An initial exploratory conversation is not charged. If an in-depth audit or technical specification is needed, its scope and fee are agreed in writing before work begins.</span></li><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><strong data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>2. Bounded Delivery Increment:</strong><span data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>We deliver the highest-priority workflow first so your team can test real functionality rather than waiting for an all-at-once launch.</span></li><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><strong data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>3. Handover &amp; Acceptance:</strong><span data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Documented testing, user guidance, and configuration sign-off before production cutover.</span></li><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><strong data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>4. Planned Support:</strong><span data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Agreed business-hours coverage, defined response expectations, and routine maintenance.</span></li></ol></div><div class="commercial-card" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><h3 data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>What to prepare before we speak</h3><ul class="commercial-list" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><strong data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>A named decision owner:</strong> One person with authority to clarify business rules, review outputs, and approve deliverables.</li><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><strong data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Representative examples:</strong> Anonymised sample records, spreadsheets, or export files that represent daily volume.</li><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><strong data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Workflow users:</strong> Access to the actual staff members who process the work day-to-day.</li><li data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><strong data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Known constraints:</strong> External audit deadlines, software renewal dates, or incumbent contracts.</li></ul></div></div><div class="faq-block" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><h3 class="faq-block__title" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Practical FAQs on terms and delivery</h3><dl class="terms-faq" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><div class="faq-item" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><dt data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>What happens if our requirements or scope change?</dt><dd data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Scope changes are normal as systems are discovered. When new requirements arise, we pause and prepare a concise written change note detailing any timing or cost adjustment. No out-of-scope work proceeds without your prior written agreement.</dd></div><div class="faq-item" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><dt data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>What is handed over upon project completion?</dt><dd data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>You receive full administration access, custom software code, data mapping sheets, runbooks, and staff guides according to the agreed contract terms. Third-party software licences (such as cloud hosting or commercial modules) remain governed by their respective vendor terms.</dd></div><div class="faq-item" data-astro-cid-uahrdstm><dt data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Are initial assessments chargeable?</dt><dd data-astro-cid-uahrdstm>Initial exploratory discussions are free. Where an organisation requires an in-depth code audit, security review, or migration feasibility specification, we define the exact deliverables and any fee upfront before any work starts.</dd></div></dl></div></div></section><section class="closing-cta"><svg class="arc-graphic arc-graphic--compact closing-cta__arc" viewBox="0 0 620 620" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25"><path d="M598 76C400 76 238 184 238 316s162 228 360 228" opacity=".16"></path><path d="M598 116C426 116 286 205 286 316s140 188 312 188" opacity=".24"></path><path d="M598 158C454 158 337 228 337 316s117 146 261 146" opacity=".38"></path><path d="M598 201C485 201 392 252 392 316s93 103 206 103" opacity=".62"></path><path d="M598 245C516 245 448 277 448 316s68 60 150 60"></path><path d="M83 316H448" opacity=".5"></path></g><circle cx="448" cy="316" r="7" fill="currentColor"></circle></svg><div class="shell closing-cta__inner"><h2>Have a project that needs clarity?</h2><a class="button button--primary" href="/contact/">Discuss your project</a></div></section></main><footer class="site-footer" data-astro-cid-nns7i3if><div class="shell footer-grid" data-astro-cid-nns7i3if><div class="footer-brand" data-astro-cid-nns7i3if><a class="brand-link" href="/" aria-label="NovaDot home" data-astro-cid-nns7i3if><img class="brand-logo" src="/brand/novadot-full-logo-dark-theme.png" srcset="/brand/novadot-full-logo-dark-theme.png 1x, /brand/novadot-full-logo-dark-theme-2x.png 2x" width="720" height="280" alt="NovaDot" data-astro-cid-nns7i3if></a><p data-astro-cid-nns7i3if>NovaDot helps UK organisations plan, build, improve and support software, systems and digital services.</p></div><div class="footer-links" data-astro-cid-nns7i3if><div data-astro-cid-nns7i3if><h2 data-astro-cid-nns7i3if>Work</h2><a href="/services/" data-astro-cid-nns7i3if>Services</a></div><div data-astro-cid-nns7i3if><h2 data-astro-cid-nns7i3if>Company</h2><a href="/events/" data-astro-cid-nns7i3if>Events &amp; Space</a><a href="/how-we-work/" data-astro-cid-nns7i3if>How We Work</a><a href="/about/" data-astro-cid-nns7i3if>About</a></div><div data-astro-cid-nns7i3if><h2 data-astro-cid-nns7i3if>Contact</h2><a href="/contact/" data-astro-cid-nns7i3if>Contact</a></div><div data-astro-cid-nns7i3if><h2 data-astro-cid-nns7i3if>Legal</h2><a href="/privacy-policy/" data-astro-cid-nns7i3if>Privacy Policy</a><a href="/terms/" data-astro-cid-nns7i3if>Terms</a></div></div></div><div class="shell footer-legal" data-astro-cid-nns7i3if><p data-astro-cid-nns7i3if>© 2026 NOVADOT LTD. Registered in England and Wales. Company number 07691369.</p></div></footer></body></html>